WEBVTT

00:01.950 --> 00:03.950
<i>So, it's starting?</i>

00:03.950 --> 00:06.350
<i>Unlike the preliminaries. which were held in a league format,</i>

00:06.350 --> 00:08.520
<i>the finals are a knockout tournament.</i>

00:08.520 --> 00:11.330
<i>If you lose once, it's all over.</i>

00:11.330 --> 00:14.360
<i>Each match is a decisive one.</i>

00:14.360 --> 00:17.060
<i>And it goes without saying that none of the teams here are weak.</i>

00:17.060 --> 00:19.030
<i>All of the matches will be difficult.</i>

00:21.510 --> 00:23.640
Hello, Wakabayashi?

00:23.640 --> 00:24.710
Oh, is it you Tsubasa?

00:24.710 --> 00:28.860
First, thank you for getting out of the group stages,

00:28.860 --> 00:29.840
just as you promised.

00:29.840 --> 00:31.920
You guys all did well!

00:31.920 --> 00:32.840
Yeah!

00:32.840 --> 00:36.000
Wakabayashi, how's the injury?

00:36.000 --> 00:38.950
I'm pretty much recovered from it, but...

00:38.950 --> 00:41.810
It looks like I'll only be able to play in a single match.

00:41.810 --> 00:43.060
Single match?

00:43.060 --> 00:47.560
Yeah, and if I'm going to play a single match, it'd of course be...

00:47.560 --> 00:48.900
The final, right?

00:48.900 --> 00:53.780
I trust you guys to make it all the way there.

00:53.780 --> 00:55.570
Got it.

00:55.570 --> 01:00.360
We also made a promise yesterday, to win this whole tournament.

01:00.360 --> 01:01.280
Yeah!

01:01.280 --> 01:04.540
So, we are counting on you being in the finals, Wakabayashi!

01:04.540 --> 01:06.640
Sure thing. See you!

01:07.520 --> 01:09.920
So you'll be going no matter what, Genzo?

01:10.670 --> 01:11.500
Yes.

01:25.020 --> 01:30.650
<i>The smell of the grass when I stumbled,</i>

01:25.070 --> 01:30.700
<i>koronda toki no shibafu no nioi</i>

01:30.650 --> 01:35.660
<i>the endless blue of the sky above...</i>

01:30.700 --> 01:35.660
<i>aogimita sora no ao hateshinakatta</i>

01:36.330 --> 01:41.500
<i>This winding, back-and-forth path</i>

01:36.330 --> 01:41.540
<i>mayotte modori susumu kidô ga</i>

01:42.210 --> 01:49.830
<i>is a map for our endless dreams</i>

01:42.210 --> 01:49.830
<i>hateshinai yume o miru boku-tachi no chizu</i>

01:49.830 --> 01:55.600
<i>Even if my hopes miss the goal</i>

01:49.830 --> 01:55.640
<i>goal o soreta kibô ga atte mo</i>

01:55.600 --> 02:04.100
<i>if I stand back up, my dreams will never end</i>

01:55.640 --> 02:04.100
<i>mata tachiagaru nara yume wa owaranai</i>

02:04.100 --> 02:09.890
<i>No.1! Race forth, faster than anyone</i>

02:04.100 --> 02:09.890
<i>No. 1! dare yori hayaku kakenuke</i>

02:09.890 --> 02:15.820
<i>Make a starting dash toward the world stage with your tricky plays!</i>

02:09.890 --> 02:15.820
<i>tricky na play de sekai e muke Start! Dash!</i>

02:15.820 --> 02:17.330
<i>Run & Run!</i>

02:17.330 --> 02:24.620
<i>Aspirations are the one buzz, buzz, buzz that gets us moving</i>

02:17.330 --> 02:24.620
<i>akogare dake ga boku-ra o chiri-chiri-chiri ugokasu yo
</i>

02:24.620 --> 02:27.540
<i>Blaze, blaze, blaze! Let's go, it's kickoff!</i>

02:24.620 --> 02:27.540
<i>mera-mera-mera iku ze kickoff</i>

02:27.540 --> 02:32.470
<i>Leap out into a giant field of dreams</i>

02:27.540 --> 02:32.470
<i>tobidasô dodekai dream field</i>

02:43.300 --> 02:47.560
<b><b>EPISODE 18:
HERE WE COME, FINALS!</b></b>

02:44.180 --> 02:46.620
<i>It's the first day of the finals!</i>

02:46.620 --> 02:50.350
<i>Every strong opponent has found its way to the finals.</i>

02:50.350 --> 02:54.910
<i>The North Hokkaido representatives, Furano Elementary, led by</i>

02:54.910 --> 02:58.530
<i>their Captain, Matsuyama, were the first ones to advance.</i>

02:59.530 --> 03:02.150
<i>The Tokyo representatives, Musashi FC, also advanced</i>

03:02.150 --> 03:06.200
<i>while having their ace, Misugi, resting on the bench.</i>

03:07.200 --> 03:10.000
<i>As for the Saitama Prefecture's representatives, Meiwa FC,</i>

03:10.000 --> 03:14.880
<i>Hyuga scored a hat-trick in just the first half.</i>

03:15.860 --> 03:22.370
<i>Just outscoring Tsubasa, he and his team have shown their worth as favorites,</i>

03:22.370 --> 03:24.950
<i>while simultaneously leading for the title of top scorer.</i>

03:24.950 --> 03:27.500
<i>In their 3rd match, however, Nankatsu SC</i>

03:27.500 --> 03:33.190
<i>has run into trouble against an unexpectedly strong opponent!</i>

03:33.190 --> 03:35.060
Go for it, Tsubasa!

03:39.360 --> 03:40.400
Again?

03:40.400 --> 03:44.780
<i>His shot was stopped once again!</i>

03:46.280 --> 03:50.740
<i>Nakanishi did not concede a single goal in the preliminaries of the tournament!</i>

03:50.740 --> 03:53.540
<i>He is being considered the number one keeper of the tournament!</i>

03:53.540 --> 03:55.430
Is that true, Manabu?

03:55.430 --> 03:59.280
Well, the Osaka representatives, Naniwa FC haven't conceded a goal in 5 matches,

03:59.280 --> 04:00.480
and didn't lose a match.

04:00.480 --> 04:02.340
They're the dark horse in this tournament,

04:02.340 --> 04:05.230
defeating strong opponents with their incredibly strong defense.

04:05.230 --> 04:06.800
What did you say?

04:10.140 --> 04:13.820
It looks like you scored a hell of a lot of goals before,

04:13.820 --> 04:16.560
but I won't be letting you score any today!

04:16.560 --> 04:18.020
Lemme tell ya!

04:18.020 --> 04:22.440
I am aiming for that record of 0 goals Wakabayashi set last year!

04:22.440 --> 04:23.780
Wha–

04:23.780 --> 04:25.490
Let's go, forwards!

04:26.040 --> 04:28.160
<i>Nakanishi kicks a long, long ball!</i>

04:28.600 --> 04:31.540
<i>The ball keeps climbing in the air!</i>

04:31.540 --> 04:32.540
What?!

04:32.540 --> 04:36.500
<i>Now, that's surprising! The ball is going directly towards Nankatsu's goal!</i>

04:37.210 --> 04:40.880
<i>Caught off guard, the front of Nankatsu's goal is unguarded!</i>

04:40.880 --> 04:43.090
All right! Just get there!

04:45.840 --> 04:47.320
<i>It's in!</i>

04:47.320 --> 04:51.600
<i>Naniwa's tall #11, Marui, scores with a header!</i>

04:52.520 --> 04:55.480
<i>It was a quick counter-attack!</i>

04:56.480 --> 04:59.850
<i>Nakanishi has a powerful kick, indeed!</i>

04:59.850 --> 05:03.480
<i>It's strong enough to compete with adults...</i>

05:03.480 --> 05:06.460
Damn, his power is monstrous!

05:06.460 --> 05:07.590
But it's just one goal!

05:07.590 --> 05:08.880
Let's stay focused!

05:08.880 --> 05:09.660
Sure!

05:10.230 --> 05:11.030
<i>But...</i>

05:11.620 --> 05:12.790
Eat this!

05:13.790 --> 05:14.910
Oh!

05:14.910 --> 05:19.290
<i>The wall in front of Naniwa's goal was thick, indeed!</i>

05:20.840 --> 05:22.460
What?!

05:24.380 --> 05:27.760
Here, forwards, go for it again!

05:28.400 --> 05:30.470
All right! Let's get another one!

05:30.470 --> 05:32.600
a wild taro appears

05:32.330 --> 05:35.430
<i>This long pass was intercepted!</i>

05:36.170 --> 05:39.140
<i>The one who cut it is Misaki, who is in great form this tournament!</i>

05:39.140 --> 05:40.810
That's Misaki for you!

05:40.810 --> 05:41.770
Damn it.

05:41.770 --> 05:45.780
<i>Now Misaki is advancing with the ball!</i>

05:45.780 --> 05:48.200
<i>The shots done until now were taken from a short distance,</i>

05:48.200 --> 05:50.580
<i>and consequently shot directly at him.</i>

05:50.580 --> 05:54.490
But with his body, he should be weak to shots at the corners!

05:54.490 --> 05:58.000
<i>Misaki aims for the low corner with a middle distance shot!</i>

05:59.140 --> 06:02.350
<i>A surprisingly agile jump to the side!</i>

06:04.380 --> 06:09.030
<i>This performance, surely as great as Wakabayashi's in his blooming era,</i>

06:09.030 --> 06:10.680
<i>comes from Taichi Nakanishi!</i>

06:10.680 --> 06:13.430
I told you I won't be conceding a goal!

06:13.430 --> 06:15.930
I am the number one keeper of this tournament!

06:15.930 --> 06:17.570
Awesome.

06:17.570 --> 06:18.990
What are you babbling about?!

06:18.990 --> 06:20.940
Spit those words after you win!

06:20.940 --> 06:22.540
Tsubasa...

06:22.540 --> 06:23.750
It's all right.

06:23.750 --> 06:24.600
What?

06:24.600 --> 06:29.280
No matter how strong he might be, there just aren't any better keepers than Wakabayashi.

06:29.280 --> 06:30.860
Wakabayashi!

06:30.860 --> 06:35.080
Yeah, there is certainly no keeper better than Wakabayashi.

06:35.080 --> 06:37.500
This time, I'll score for sure!

06:37.500 --> 06:42.040
<i>Naniwa switches to the offensive with a long throw from keeper, Nakanishi!</i>

06:42.040 --> 06:44.170
Damn, they're underestimating us!

06:44.170 --> 06:46.170
Takayanagi, pass the ball to the left!

06:46.170 --> 06:47.880
Okay!

06:47.880 --> 06:50.010
Shirai, connect the ball to the sides!

06:51.120 --> 06:52.390
<i>It's brilliant!</i>

06:52.390 --> 06:54.530
<i>Precise orders are coming from Nakanishi.</i>

06:54.530 --> 06:59.460
<i>Yes! Since keepers are placed at the back line, they can observe other players' moves the best!</i>

06:59.460 --> 07:01.640
Send a pass to the front line!

07:02.730 --> 07:05.270
<i>The ball is headed for Ogami, the forward!</i>

07:05.850 --> 07:09.740
<i>Oh! Tsubasa, the center forward, has come back to steal the ball himself!</i>

07:11.110 --> 07:12.990
Ogami, pass the ball to left!

07:13.460 --> 07:14.210
Okay!

07:14.210 --> 07:15.700
Ishizaki, cut to the right!

07:15.700 --> 07:16.740
Got it!

07:17.340 --> 07:19.290
<i>Ishizaki intercepts the pass!</i>

07:19.290 --> 07:22.250
<i>Tsubasa is one step ahead of Nakanishi's orders!</i>

07:22.250 --> 07:22.900
What?!

07:22.900 --> 07:23.580
We did it!

07:23.580 --> 07:25.750
Take this, Kisugi!

07:26.820 --> 07:28.000
Nice pass!

07:28.000 --> 07:31.590
Looks like I finally did something good for the team.

07:31.590 --> 07:33.840
Maeda, strengthen the right wing!

07:33.840 --> 07:35.090
Sure!

07:35.090 --> 07:37.260
Oh, the pass goes there though.

07:37.750 --> 07:38.680
Aw, crap!

07:39.310 --> 07:42.230
All right! This time, I'll score for sure!

07:42.230 --> 07:45.810
That's right, there simply isn't a better keeper than Wakabayashi!

07:45.810 --> 07:48.520
Wakabayashi wouldn't make that kind of mistake!

07:48.520 --> 07:51.280
We'll back Tsubasa up, too!

07:51.280 --> 07:53.650
Damn! Get around him, guys!

07:53.650 --> 07:56.440
Block that squirt's approach!

07:56.440 --> 07:57.120
Yes!

07:57.120 --> 08:00.540
<i>Naniwa's well-organized defense is waiting for him up front.</i>

08:00.540 --> 08:01.830
Tsubasa!

08:01.830 --> 08:03.580
Behind you!

08:03.580 --> 08:06.980
<i>Tsubasa passes the ball back and breaks into a run!</i>

08:06.980 --> 08:07.880
Take this!

08:07.880 --> 08:09.660
<i>An excellent one-two play!</i>

08:09.660 --> 08:12.130
<i>Even Naniwa can't read their movements.</i>

08:12.130 --> 08:15.650
<i>They come from different elementary schools, and they used to be adversaries.</i>

08:15.650 --> 08:19.040
<i>But, here and now, they are already in perfect harmony.</i>

08:19.040 --> 08:21.640
<i>Nankatsu SC is a good team.</i>

08:21.640 --> 08:24.140
<i>Tsubasa is in a one-on-one with the goalkeeper.</i>

08:24.140 --> 08:25.060
Come at me!

08:25.060 --> 08:29.250
<i>He gets in position to shoot from outside the penalty area!</i>

08:29.250 --> 08:30.770
<i>That's too soon!</i>

08:30.770 --> 08:31.780
<i>What a waste!</i>

08:32.260 --> 08:35.200
<i>As if any other goalkeeper could surpass Wakabayashi!</i>

08:35.200 --> 08:37.030
<i>I'll score from where I'm standing!</i>

08:39.370 --> 08:41.370
Are you stupid?! Your shot was too early!

08:41.880 --> 08:42.830
I got it!

08:44.210 --> 08:47.460
<i>Nakanishi catches it firmly with both hands...</i>

08:48.510 --> 08:50.210
<i>No! It slips out!</i>

08:50.210 --> 08:52.300
<i>Goal!</i>

08:52.300 --> 08:54.220
<i>It pierces in to the goal!</i>

08:54.890 --> 08:55.840
Yes!

08:55.840 --> 08:58.820
<i>The ball had an incredibly rotation effect!</i>

08:58.820 --> 09:00.930
<i>Nankatsu has caught up with Naniwa!</i>

09:00.930 --> 09:03.240
All right! You did it, Tsubasa!

09:03.240 --> 09:05.120
So, he shot from outside of the penalty area?

09:05.120 --> 09:05.940
Eh?

09:05.940 --> 09:10.880
Speaking of which, Tsubasa stole two goals from you during the inter-school tournament,

09:10.880 --> 09:13.780
but you didn't concede a single goal from outside of the penalty area.

09:14.690 --> 09:19.780
Tsubasa wants to prove it. He wants to prove this goalkeeper isn't as skilled as you.

09:19.780 --> 09:25.290
And with this, he won't be able to break your record from last year.

09:25.290 --> 09:28.960
Damn... that Tsubasa!

09:28.960 --> 09:32.670
You're awesome, Tsubasa!

09:32.670 --> 09:35.250
<i>With Tsubasa's goal, we're all tied up, 1-1!</i>

09:35.250 --> 09:37.170
<i>Nankatsu's offense has livened up!</i>

09:37.170 --> 09:40.620
<i>Misaki steadily attacks while skillfully controlling the ball!</i>

09:40.620 --> 09:43.060
<i>Nankatsu's forwards are gathering in front of the goal.</i>

09:44.190 --> 09:46.930
<i>The ball goes to Tsubasa.</i>

09:46.930 --> 09:50.610
Damn! Like hell I'd let you score another one on me!

09:50.610 --> 09:53.110
I'll stop you with my entire body!

09:54.940 --> 09:55.650
What?!

09:55.650 --> 09:57.990
<i>Kisugi is unmarked! He shoots!</i>

09:59.080 --> 10:00.280
<i>Here it is!</i>

10:00.280 --> 10:02.770
<i>Nankatsu has reversed the score!</i>

10:02.770 --> 10:04.080
We did it!

10:05.320 --> 10:06.580
<i>The first half ends!</i>

10:06.580 --> 10:08.680
<i>Nankatsu, who have put overwhelming pressure on their opponents</i>

10:08.680 --> 10:11.960
<i>are in the lead against Naniwa with a score of 2-1!</i>

10:13.590 --> 10:16.010
All right! Keep this up, guys!

10:16.010 --> 10:16.750
Yes!

10:16.750 --> 10:19.380
Well, even my shot got in!

10:19.380 --> 10:21.430
Our opponent's goalkeeper is not scary at all.

10:22.020 --> 10:24.450
What's wrong with Nakanishi?

10:24.450 --> 10:26.110
He conceded 2 goals...

10:26.110 --> 10:27.250
Yes.

10:27.250 --> 10:30.060
<i>They scored 2 goals against me.</i>

10:32.570 --> 10:35.190
<i>Frankly, it's not Naniwa's goalkeepers's fault.</i>

10:35.190 --> 10:37.760
<i>Nankatsu is just that strong.</i>

10:37.760 --> 10:41.820
<i>They've already improved from the time they played against us...</i>

10:41.820 --> 10:46.540
<i>Even in the second half, Nankatsu's attack continued.</i>

10:46.540 --> 10:51.370
<i>Ever since this tournament began, the team's level has steadily kept rising.</i>

10:51.370 --> 10:57.880
<i>Tsubasa must have realized that, so he is involving his teammates as much as he can.</i>

10:57.880 --> 11:01.130
<i>You have grown so much, Tsubasa.</i>

11:01.920 --> 11:03.680
<i>It's the fourth goal for Nankatsu!</i>

11:03.680 --> 11:05.920
<i>Nevertheless, Nakanishi looks like he's lost all of his spirit</i>

11:05.920 --> 11:09.220
<i>after conceding goal after goal to Nankatsu.</i>

11:09.220 --> 11:10.310
Damn it...

11:10.310 --> 11:14.310
<i>It looks like I've completely lost...</i>

11:14.310 --> 11:18.900
<i>But you, Tsubasa Ozora... you've gone so far so as to embarrass me here.</i>

11:18.900 --> 11:21.820
<i>I'll make you pay!</i>

11:21.820 --> 11:24.570
<i>Tsubasa swiftly closes in on the goal!</i>

11:26.200 --> 11:28.290
<i>Tsubasa gets ready to shoot!</i>

11:28.290 --> 11:33.080
I'm gonna take that golden right leg of yours!

11:33.500 --> 11:36.100
Eat this!

11:36.750 --> 11:41.420
<i>Tsubasa evades Nakanishi's charge by a hair's width!</i>

11:45.850 --> 11:48.040
<i>It's an excellent goal!</i>

11:48.040 --> 11:51.810
<i>5-1! This goal from Tsubasa is the final nail in Naniwa's coffin!</i>

11:51.810 --> 11:53.810
We did it!

11:56.540 --> 12:00.680
Nakanishi! Maybe if you'd gone for the ball instead with that intensity,

12:00.680 --> 12:02.870
you would've stopped that last one.

12:10.910 --> 12:13.620
I... have completely lost.

12:15.530 --> 12:17.720
<i>The game</i>

12:17.720 --> 12:20.130
<i>Nankatsu is among the best eight!</i>

12:19.170 --> 12:20.130
SIGN: NANKATSU SC:5 - 1: Naniwa FC

12:20.130 --> 12:21.210
One, two...

12:21.210 --> 12:23.440
You did it, Nankatsu!

12:23.440 --> 12:25.380
Go and become champions!

12:25.380 --> 12:28.220
<i>Nankatsu SC just keeps getting stronger and stronger.</i>

12:28.220 --> 12:30.980
<i>You just can't take your eyes off of this team.</i>

12:31.850 --> 12:34.660
As expected of the captain.

12:34.660 --> 12:39.230
Tsubasa has really managed to become  the pillar of this team and keep everything balanced.

12:39.230 --> 12:44.740
It looks like we won't be able to defeat Nankatsu unless I play full time.

12:45.290 --> 12:46.490
Captain...

12:56.920 --> 13:01.370
<i>In the quarter-finals tomorrow, the best 4 among the 8 teams</i>

13:01.370 --> 13:03.130
<i>who have won the group the stage will be decided.</i>

13:04.180 --> 13:10.260
<i>Meiwa FC and Furano Elementary have made it through their fierce matches and continue on!</i>

13:04.650 --> 13:05.290
SIGN: MEIWA FC: 5 - 1: KOZAI ELEMENTARY

13:08.220 --> 13:10.260
SIGN: FURANO ELEMENTARY: 3 - 1: BIZEN FC

13:10.260 --> 13:14.330
<i>Our boys at Nankatsu have faced Shinjo, heavily outscoring them</i>

13:13.290 --> 13:17.600
SIGN: NANKATSU SC: 7 - 0: SHINJO FC

13:14.330 --> 13:17.600
<i>and securing a place for themselves in the best four.</i>

13:17.600 --> 13:19.600
You did well, guys.

13:19.600 --> 13:22.950
The winner of Musashi vs. Hitachi, which is  to take place now,

13:22.950 --> 13:25.610
will be our opponent tomorrow.

13:25.610 --> 13:27.880
Well, it only makes sense...

13:27.880 --> 13:30.250
Musashi will probably win it if everthing goes as usual, won't they?

13:30.250 --> 13:30.950
You're right.

13:30.950 --> 13:34.590
Musashi FC are the reigning powerhouse from Kanto.

13:34.590 --> 13:38.210
Their regular players are elites chosen from a group of 1,000 players.

13:38.210 --> 13:43.840
On the team, their standout player is their Captain, Jun Misugi.

13:43.840 --> 13:46.630
His high technical skill is so superior to the elementary school level,

13:46.630 --> 13:49.200
that other players can hardly make physical contact, much less beat him.

13:49.200 --> 13:51.160
And because of that elegant play style...

13:51.160 --> 13:54.470
"The Young Noble of the Field". That's what they call him, right, coach?

13:54.470 --> 13:55.620
Wow!

13:55.620 --> 13:59.910
But you know, he hasn't played a single match in this tournament yet.

13:59.910 --> 14:01.610
Maybe he's injured or something.

14:01.610 --> 14:03.830
He's not. I don't know why he does it,

14:03.830 --> 14:07.440
but Misugi has always been known for rarely playing in games.

14:07.440 --> 14:08.110
What...?

14:08.110 --> 14:10.110
And that's why the girls are so crazy about him! Like,

14:10.110 --> 14:15.680
"Oh my god, Misugi is so mysterious! How awesome!"

14:15.680 --> 14:17.620
It looks like he's just putting on airs to me.

14:17.620 --> 14:23.260
Thanks to Musashi's power as a unit, they managed to easily get past the group stages,

14:23.260 --> 14:27.280
but if it's us they're playing against, they'll be sure to have Misugi play.

14:27.280 --> 14:28.850
That's what I've been waiting for.

14:28.850 --> 14:31.700
We'll win and advance to the final!

14:31.700 --> 14:33.510
For Wakabayashi's sake too!

14:33.510 --> 14:34.850
Yeah!

14:34.850 --> 14:36.650
Hey, Misugi!

14:36.650 --> 14:38.650
The semi-finals are upon us.

14:38.650 --> 14:41.110
Misugi, do you plan to play?

14:41.110 --> 14:42.880
Well, who knows...

14:42.880 --> 14:47.690
If you win, you'll be playing against the champion contender, Nankatsu SC, next.

14:47.690 --> 14:51.190
Nankatsu is strong. Especially Tsubasa Ozora.

14:51.190 --> 14:54.520
I'd very much like to have a contest of skills with him.

14:54.520 --> 14:55.050
Oh?

14:55.050 --> 14:56.700
So we can be sure that you'll play, then?

14:56.700 --> 15:00.560
Oh no, Misugi won't play at all until the match against Nankatsu?

15:00.560 --> 15:03.270
But if the team gets into a pinch, he might even play today.

15:03.270 --> 15:06.710
So we need to have the opponent team work hard! Hitachi FC!

15:06.710 --> 15:12.470
Hooray! Hooray! Hitachi!

15:12.470 --> 15:16.980
Damn that Misugi! He makes it look like we don't even exist.

15:16.980 --> 15:19.060
Let's show him what we're capable of!

15:19.520 --> 15:21.810
What do you mean, Misugi?

15:21.810 --> 15:26.360
Coach, this tournament is very special for me.

15:26.360 --> 15:28.480
You know it very well, don't you?

15:29.860 --> 15:33.610
I know myself the best.

15:33.610 --> 15:37.400
Do you really want to play against Tsubasa Ozora that badly?

15:37.400 --> 15:38.290
Yes.

15:38.290 --> 15:41.200
Well, I can't say I don't understand how you feel...

15:41.200 --> 15:43.580
But I can't let you play that easily.

15:44.000 --> 15:48.090
For today, you will sit quietly on the bench. We'll talk more after that.

15:48.640 --> 15:49.910
Understood.

15:54.640 --> 15:56.140
Manager?

15:57.430 --> 15:58.470
Whew...

15:58.470 --> 16:01.680
This is match is super crowded too.

16:01.680 --> 16:05.100
It shows how much attention Musashi FC is garnering.

16:05.100 --> 16:06.580
Tsubasa!

16:07.570 --> 16:09.300
Yayoi!

16:09.300 --> 16:11.820
I need to talk to you for a moment.

16:14.320 --> 16:17.440
Will we take another trip via truck...?

16:17.440 --> 16:17.870
What?!

16:20.790 --> 16:23.290
Tsubasa is with that girl?!

16:23.290 --> 16:25.750
What are they discussing by themselves...?!

16:25.750 --> 16:26.670
Tsubasa!

16:27.490 --> 16:28.600
I'm so jealo—

16:28.600 --> 16:30.150
No, I can't forgive this!

16:30.150 --> 16:32.420
I haven't even touched him yet!

16:32.420 --> 16:34.120
I'm begging you, Tsubasa!

16:34.120 --> 16:36.350
Let our captain win!

16:36.350 --> 16:39.930
To tell you the truth, he has a heart condition that won't let him play football anymore!

16:39.930 --> 16:41.020
What?!

16:41.290 --> 16:42.180
What?!

16:42.560 --> 16:45.190
He can't play football?

16:45.190 --> 16:51.590
His doctors are trying to stop him, but he insists on playing until the tournament ends.

16:51.590 --> 16:53.960
Is that why he hasn't played any matches?

16:53.960 --> 16:57.410
Only the coach and I know about this.

16:58.870 --> 17:03.360
Please! This is the last tournament of his life!

17:03.360 --> 17:07.170
So whatever happens, please, let him win tomorrow's match!

17:07.170 --> 17:08.560
I can't do that.

17:08.560 --> 17:10.920
Tsubasa...

17:10.920 --> 17:14.710
Winning this tournament is part of my dream.

17:14.710 --> 17:18.590
If I do, it's decided that I'll go to Brazil with Roberto.

17:18.590 --> 17:20.770
What? Brazil?

17:20.770 --> 17:23.890
Yes... Brazil, the land of football!

17:23.890 --> 17:27.690
Then I'll grow to be a professional football player there.

17:27.690 --> 17:31.360
So, whoever my opponent is, I can't afford to lose!

17:32.190 --> 17:37.360
I also think that Misugi will be much happier if I play my best against him.

17:37.360 --> 17:39.490
Tsubasa...

17:44.040 --> 17:49.420
<i>Goal! Hitachi finally make their comeback in the 5th minute of the second half.</i>

17:49.420 --> 17:51.420
We did it! We did it!

17:51.860 --> 17:53.340
Coach! I'm going!

17:54.100 --> 17:56.310
Misugi...

17:56.310 --> 18:00.180
If we lose and everything ends here, I won't be able to play against Nankatsu.

18:00.180 --> 18:01.470
Please.

18:02.030 --> 18:02.890
It can't be helped.

18:02.890 --> 18:06.560
But the moment you look bad out there, I'm bringing you back here immediately.

18:06.560 --> 18:08.020
Thank you so much!

18:08.020 --> 18:10.520
<i>Musashi, who have fallen into this disadvantageous position,</i>

18:10.520 --> 18:15.030
<i>are bringing in their ace Misugi on for Yamamoto.</i>

18:15.030 --> 18:18.030
Misugi!

18:18.030 --> 18:19.380
Captain!

18:19.380 --> 18:20.920
Captain, take this.

18:20.920 --> 18:21.700
Yes.

18:21.700 --> 18:24.490
Misugi's finally out on the field.

18:25.110 --> 18:27.000
Misugi...

18:28.710 --> 18:30.960
Misugi! Do your best!

18:36.800 --> 18:38.670
<i>The ball finds its mark!</i>

18:38.670 --> 18:42.040
<i>This boy is Musashi's #14, Jun Misugi.</i>

18:42.040 --> 18:44.320
<i>It wouldn't be an exaggeration to say that Musashi's play</i>

18:44.320 --> 18:47.430
<i>begins and ends with Misugi.</i>

18:47.430 --> 18:49.490
Damn, so what if he's Misugi?

18:49.490 --> 18:51.280
No matter how great they say he is—

18:51.280 --> 18:53.230
isn't he just a kid our age?!

18:53.940 --> 18:55.900
<i>His dribbles are so fluid!</i>

18:55.900 --> 18:56.360
What?!

18:56.360 --> 18:58.720
<i>His footwork is magnificent!</i>

18:58.720 --> 19:02.030
<i>It's as if the players around him were frozen in place! What a strange sight!</i>

19:02.030 --> 19:04.030
Misugi!

19:05.490 --> 19:06.890
<i>GOOOOOOOOOOAL!</i>

19:06.890 --> 19:09.540
<i>Misugi ties the game with this shot!</i>

19:09.540 --> 19:10.790
SIGN: MUSASHI FC: 2 - 2: HITACHI FC

19:10.790 --> 19:13.790
<i>He goes straight for the tie in the blink of an eye! This is great!</i>

19:14.170 --> 19:16.800
<i>This is the true face of Musashi!</i>

19:17.660 --> 19:20.250
<i>Musashi's forwards are all pressing the attack!</i>

19:20.250 --> 19:22.800
<i>Musashi is dominating the pace of the game!</i>

19:22.800 --> 19:23.890
Ichinose!

19:25.100 --> 19:27.010
Pass it to Honma in the wing right away!

19:27.010 --> 19:27.930
Okay!

19:27.930 --> 19:29.820
Give it back to Sanada in the mid-field!

19:29.820 --> 19:30.520
All right!

19:30.520 --> 19:35.290
<i>With his dribbling, pass work and ability to control the game,</i>

19:35.290 --> 19:37.970
<i>Misugi is proving why he's the keystone of Musashi.</i>

19:39.190 --> 19:40.690
Sanada, on your back!

19:40.690 --> 19:41.490
Okay!

19:41.490 --> 19:42.140
Captain!

19:42.140 --> 19:45.240
<i>Misugi runs forward and takes a long shot himself!</i>

19:47.120 --> 19:49.350
<i>Goal! In the 10th minute of the second half.</i>

19:49.350 --> 19:51.750
<i>Musashi's strikes brilliantly in the blink of an eye!</i>

19:52.250 --> 19:55.170
<i>And yet, the level of Misugi's play continues to escalate.</i>

19:55.170 --> 19:57.360
<i>He really is the Young Noble of the Field!</i>

19:57.360 --> 19:58.050
<i>This is awesome.</i>

19:58.050 --> 20:02.050
<i>He can play like that even with a heart disease?</i>

20:02.970 --> 20:04.550
<i>The match is over!</i>

20:05.490 --> 20:10.630
<i>In the last match of the quarter-finals, Musashi has defeated Hitachi, 6-2.</i>

20:10.630 --> 20:14.810
<i>With this, we'll finally see Nankatsu and Musashi's match!</i>

20:15.920 --> 20:19.150
<i>Tsubasa, I'll finally get to play against you.</i>

20:20.190 --> 20:21.630
<i>Misugi...</i>

20:23.560 --> 20:27.520
Manager, did you go to see Tsubasa earlier?

20:27.520 --> 20:28.910
Yes...

20:28.910 --> 20:33.510
You didn't tell him about my heart condition, did you?

20:33.510 --> 20:37.670
Of course not! I was asking him how he was doing.

20:37.670 --> 20:42.170
You know, I learned that Tsubasa will go to Brazil if he wins the tournament.

20:42.170 --> 20:43.460
Brazil?

20:43.460 --> 20:49.300
Yes! Tsubasa says that he'll go to Brazil and become a professional football player.

20:49.300 --> 20:52.300
I see. That's just like Tsubasa.

20:52.300 --> 20:54.350
That's a wonderful dream.

20:54.350 --> 20:59.150
They say Tsubasa's never been apart from the ball since he was a child.

20:59.150 --> 21:03.840
His play style has a high ceiling, which really lets him exhibit his skills freely.

21:03.840 --> 21:07.820
And above all, Tsubasa absolutely loves football.

21:07.820 --> 21:10.600
I'm sure Tsubasa can surpass Japan's borders

21:10.600 --> 21:13.350
and become a known football player across the world.

21:13.350 --> 21:14.750
Thank you, manager.

21:14.750 --> 21:17.530
I'm getting more and more fired up.

21:17.530 --> 21:21.250
I'll finally be able to play against Tsubasa tomorrow.

21:21.340 --> 21:25.010
It might be the last match I ever play.

21:26.260 --> 21:29.190
I'll play the full time tomorrow.

21:29.190 --> 21:32.770
There's no way we'll be able to defeat Tsubasa if I don't.

21:32.770 --> 21:35.120
Of course, I'm confident that we'll be able  to win.

21:35.120 --> 21:38.300
However, even if it means I can't play in the final because of it,

21:38.300 --> 21:39.860
there's no helping it.

21:41.770 --> 21:44.330
I'll play with everything I've got.

21:44.330 --> 21:47.530
I'll leave everything on the pitch in tomorrow's match!

21:50.370 --> 21:52.930
Nankatsu vs. Musashi.

21:52.930 --> 21:56.870
It'll be troublesome for us no matter who wins.

21:56.870 --> 22:00.300
But before that, we have to deal with Furano tomorrow.

22:07.370 --> 22:10.340
But our missing piece is finally here.

22:11.760 --> 22:15.600
With this, victory will certainly belong to Meiwa.

22:38.790 --> 22:44.670
<i>chotto are mi na ace ga tooru</i>

22:38.790 --> 22:44.670
<i>Hey, look over there at the ace passing through</i>

22:44.670 --> 22:50.680
<i>suguremono zo to machijû sawagu</i>

22:44.670 --> 22:50.680
<i>He's the best, and the whole town cheers him on</i>

22:50.680 --> 22:56.680
<i>chô-chô samba, zigzag samba</i>

22:50.680 --> 22:56.680
<i>Butterfly samba, zig-zag samba</i>

22:56.680 --> 23:02.150
<i>aitsu no uwasa de chamba mo hashiru</i>

22:56.680 --> 23:02.150
<i>Even little old ladies go around talking about him</i>

23:03.110 --> 23:08.280
<i>sore ni tsukete mo ore-tacha nan na no</i>

23:03.110 --> 23:08.280
<i>So, even if we have him, who are we?</i>

23:09.200 --> 23:14.990
<i>ball hitotsu ni kiri-kiri mai sa</i>

23:09.200 --> 23:14.990
<i>The ball spins round and round</i>

23:14.990 --> 23:21.040
<i>Dash, dash, dash! Kick and dash!</i>

23:21.040 --> 23:26.050
<i>itsuka kimeru ze inazuma shoot</i>

23:21.040 --> 23:26.050
<i>One day, I'll score with a lightning shot!</i>

23:27.340 --> 23:33.220
<i>son toki ore ga super hero sa</i>

23:27.340 --> 23:33.220
<i>When that happens, I'll become a super hero!</i>

23:33.220 --> 23:39.100
<i>Dash, dash, dash! Kick and dash!</i>

23:39.100 --> 23:45.980
<i>moete seishun kakenukero</i>

23:39.100 --> 23:45.980
<i>This fierce youth is on the field!</i>

23:50.070 --> 24:00.640
COMING UP, EPISODE 19:
FIERCE FIGHT! MEIWA VS. FURANO
